Downloaded when building
------------------------

F-Droid
  apps/web/scripts/download-android-apps.sh downloads the F-Droid client
  1.17.0 from f-droid.org, unmodified, to be installed on the Android devices
  Doppelganger runs. GNU GPL version 3 or later. Source:
  https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/-/tree/1.17.0

Chromium
  The same script downloads ChromePublic.apk and SystemWebView.apk, Chromium
  158.0.8127.0, from Chromium's official snapshot build 1727462, unmodified,
  to be installed on the same devices. Chromium is under a BSD-style license,
  with components under other licenses, including the GNU LGPL. Source:
  https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/88c3ce436c686bd2114720debffedcb893ca464a

Inter
  The site's typeface, downloaded from Google Fonts when the site is built
  and served with it. Copyright 2016 The Inter Project Authors
  (https://github.com/rsms/inter). SIL Open Font License 1.1.

npm packages
  The Docker image contains the npm packages that apps/web depends on, each
  with its own license file in node_modules. The site's /licenses page lists
  them. Two need attribution here:
  - caniuse-lite, by Ben Briggs, with data from https://caniuse.com by Alexis
    Deveria. Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.
  - @img/sharp-libvips, the libvips image library and its dependencies, built
